Subject: wifi: mac80211: rearm station TXQs after failed link activation

A driver can dequeue a shared station TXQ while valid_links temporarily
includes the new link. On callback failure the old mask is restored only
after the callback returns, so waking in the callback can be premature.
Reschedule buffered TXQs after mask and link cleanup, preserving PS/AQL
checks and the original activation error. Reuse the existing BH/RCU-protected
schedule-and-wake contract from the aggregation path.

This fixes the conditional rollback path; it does not establish the cause
of an observed firmware or client power-save stall.

--- a/net/mac80211/sta_info.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/sta_info.c
@@ -3495,8 +3495,24 @@
 	ret = drv_change_sta_links(sdata->local, sdata, &sta->sta,
 				   old_links, new_links);
 	if (ret) {
+		int i;
+
 		sta->sta.valid_links = old_links;
 		sta_remove_link(sta, link_id, false);
+
+		/* A driver may have stopped a shared TXQ while the temporary
+		 * link mask was visible. Rearm after the rollback is complete.
+		 */
+		local_bh_disable();
+		rcu_read_lock();
+		for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(sta->sta.txq); i++) {
+			if (!sta->sta.txq[i] || !txq_has_queue(sta->sta.txq[i]))
+				continue;
+			schedule_and_wake_txq(sdata->local,
+					      to_txq_info(sta->sta.txq[i]));
+		}
+		rcu_read_unlock();
+		local_bh_enable();
 		return ret;
 	}
 
